# Godot AI

The Godot veneer has the free MIT plugin Godot AI (`godot/addons/godot_ai`). It connects Cursor to the open Godot editor: scene, undoable edits, play, input, logs, and a screenshot of the running game. Prefer it over editing blind and relaunching when the tools are available.

The editor has to be open. `./scripts/godot-up.sh` alone is not connected. The shared client entry is `.cursor/mcp.json` (telemetry off). Setup is in `godot/README.md` under "Godot AI (editor connection)". A new machine still needs `uv` on the path and one Cursor reload.

`game_eval` pastes its code inside one function. Do not declare a nested `func` there. Godot treats that as a standalone lambda, `reload()` aborts, and a debug play session parks in the remote debugger until play is stopped and started again. OTP state survives that restart.

## Host scenarios

A repeatable Godot beat is a JSON file in `godot/scenarios/`, run by `./scripts/godot-scenario.sh`. `helen-alice` is Helen's key paper, W0 (PIN `13579`), Alice's public slip given to seated Helen, W1, Exit session, Alice's key paper, and login with the PIN W1 printed. Run it after `./scripts/session-up.sh` while genesis is still open and port 24567 is free. Do not combine it with `session-up --godot` (that occupies the port). `GODOT_SCENARIO_WINDOW=1` leaves the window open. That launch is detached; if the shell is aborted, read `lab/run/scenario.log` and `lab/run/scenario.pid`. Detail is in `godot/README.md` under "Host scenarios". Use that script for this beat. Do not re-drive it as a string of `game_eval` calls. A clean run on 2026-11-22 took 53 seconds after `session-up` had already finished. The script writes the PINs from a successful run to `lab/run/scenario-pins.txt` (gitignored, kept across `session-down`). When asked for a PIN, read that file and answer from it. Do not guess. If you drive genesis or W1 by hand, write the same fields there: scenario, when, helen_pin, alice_pin, session, principal_id. Say that the file is the last run when the lab has since been wiped. `./scripts/godot-playbook.sh` is still the known red peer path, not this beat.
